CARSHARING 2017 DEMAND & WEATHER REPORT
SQL Analysis Report for the Marketing Team
Executive Summary

The 2017 CarSharing analysis identified clear demand patterns across time and weather conditions. The highest recorded demand rate was 6.46 on 15 June 2017 at 17:00. Saturday recorded the highest average demand among the weekday comparison at 4.61, July was the strongest month at 4.91, and Fall was the strongest season at 4.77.
Mild conditions were the most frequently observed temperature category at 48.64%, while Clear or partly cloudy was the most common weather condition at 67.28%. Hot conditions recorded the highest average demand at 4.97, compared with 4.13 for Mild and 3.37 for Cold. These findings provide a basis for timing campaigns and operational resources around periods of stronger observed demand.
